  "extraction_notes": [
    "BSS84P is the datasheet identity for the requested BSS84PH6327 ordering variant; it is a p-channel enhancement MOSFET.",
    "All extracted electrical values and curve coordinates are positive magnitudes while conditions preserve the datasheet's negative p-channel signs.",
    "The electrical table lists VGS(th) = -1 V minimum, -1.5 V typical, and -2 V maximum at VGS = VDS and ID = -20 uA.",
    "The electrical table lists RDS(on) at VGS = -4.5 V, ID = -0.14 A and VGS = -10 V, ID = -0.17 A; all typical and maximum values are preserved.",
    "The p. 5 to p. 7 curves were read directly from the supplied figures. Curve conditions are included exactly where printed and explicitly marked when not stated on a figure.",
    "The electrical table lists Ciss maximum 19 pF, Coss maximum 8 pF, and Crss maximum 3 pF in addition to the typical values recorded in specs; the strict schema has one field for each capacitance.",
    "The electrical table lists reverse-recovery time trr typical 23 ns and maximum 34 ns at VR = -30 V, IF = IS, diF/dt = 100 A/us, and reverse-recovery charge Qrr typical 10 nC and maximum 15 nC; the strict schema has no reverse-recovery field for MOSFETs.",
    "The electrical table lists VSD typical -0.93 V and maximum -1.24 V at VGS = 0 V, IF = -0.17 A; the maximum magnitude is recorded in the body-diode field."
  ],
